<title>USA: U.S. funds show outflow for three-day period.</title>
<headline>U.S. funds show outflow for three-day period.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA ROSA, Calif. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. mutual funds showed an outflow of $400 million for the three day period ended October 17 versus an inflow of $4.7 billion for the two day period ended October 14, according to a survey by a mutual fund tracking firm.</p>
<p>U.S. stock funds recorded an inflow of $500 million a slowdown from an inflow of $3.4 billion for the previous two day period. Bond showed an outflow of $600 million versus an inflow of $100 million for the two day period ended October 14, according to Mutual Fund Trim Tabs.</p>
